L1: // deploy.mjs — `uika deploy status|install|uninstall|adopt|targets|auto|hook-run` (ADR-0051/0052).
L2: // Commit-triggered distribution: when a commit touches the estate's skills, law, or registries,
L3: // push the changed surfaces out to this machine's consumers — every harness skill home, the
L4: // adopted repos' repo-local homes and marked law blocks — while
L5: // reporting the legs that stay owner-applied (MCP/models are render-only, ADR-0017).
L6: // New projects adopt themselves: a global git `init.templateDir` plants the post-commit hook in
L7: // every repository created on this machine, and the hook adopts a repo on its first commit when
L8: // it is a local project (root commit, no origin remote). Auto-adopted repos are recorded in
L9: // data/deploy/targets.json (machine-local) and join the deploy fan-out.
L10: // Dry-run by default; writes only with --apply. The post-commit hook runs `deploy hook-run`,
L11: // always exits 0, and records actions in data/deploy/deploy.log.
